== nine_iron
  cast: NineIron, Player
  setting: NineIronHide

INT. A MAINTENANCE LOCKER, THREE FLOORS DOWN

NineIron is missing the lower half of their left arm and has replaced
it with a length of rebar wrapped in cloth tape. Hence the name.

NINEIRON
  You picked a side. Good. The Motherboard can't read you yet — it
  reads commitments. Until you commit, you're noise.

  Now. The thing you need to understand: there is no chatter-mod war.
  There is a Motherboard, and there is everyone else. The "war" is the
  attention budget the Motherboard needs us to spend so it can spend
  ours.

* Why are you telling me?
  -> nine_iron_why
* I want to destroy it.
  -> nine_iron_plan_destroy
* I want to join it.
  -> nine_iron_plan_join
* I want to expose it — make the chatters and mods unite.
  -> nine_iron_plan_unite

== nine_iron_why
  cast: NineIron, Player

NINEIRON
  Because I was a cyborg for six months and I remember it. That isn't
  supposed to happen. Whatever they did to me, it didn't take all the
  way. I am, in their words, a defective node.

  And defective nodes get pruned. So I'm picking my exit.

* I want to destroy it.
  -> nine_iron_plan_destroy
* I want to join it.
  -> nine_iron_plan_join
* I want to unite the factions against it.
  -> nine_iron_plan_unite
* I'm not the right person for this.
  -> nine_iron_refuse

== nine_iron_plan_destroy
  cast: NineIron, Player

NINEIRON
  Then you'll need a key. Two keys, technically — one from each
  faction's leadership. They don't know they have them. The chatters'
  is in Vex's sticker book. The mods' is in Praxis's wall of monitors,
  the one labeled CALIBRATION.

<if: Vex.knows.player_signed_chatter>
  Vex trusts you enough. Probably.
<else if: Praxis.knows.player_signed_mod>
  Praxis trusts you enough. Probably.
<else>
  You haven't earned either trust yet. You'll have to fix that.
<-

<set: NineIron.knows.player_knows_motherboard = true>

* Go to Vex.
  -> chatter_camp
* Go to Praxis.
  -> mod_outpost
* Skip the keys. Just go to the Motherboard.
  -> motherboard_intro

== nine_iron_plan_join
  cast: NineIron, Player

NINEIRON
  (long silence)
  ...Why.

  No. Don't tell me. I don't want it on me. The door is in the plaza,
  behind the fountain. Push it. It opens. Tell the Motherboard I sent
  you. It won't help, but I'd like it to know.

* Go to the door.
  -> motherboard_intro
* Reconsider.
  -> nine_iron

== nine_iron_plan_unite
  cast: NineIron, Player

NINEIRON
  Hard road. Hardest road. Vex has to believe Praxis. Praxis has to
  believe Vex. Both have to believe me.

  You'd need both sides to have seen a cyborg with their own eyes. Not
  rumor. Sight.

<if: Vex.knows.saw_cyborg>
  <if: Praxis.knows.saw_cyborg>
    Both leaders already suspect. You can sell this.
  <else>
    Vex suspects. Praxis still doesn't. Show her.
  <-
<else>
  <if: Praxis.knows.saw_cyborg>
    Praxis suspects. Vex doesn't. Show him.
  <else>
    Neither leader believes. You'll have to convince them both.
  <-
<-

* Go to Vex.
  -> chatter_camp
* Go to Praxis.
  -> mod_outpost
* Go straight to the Motherboard and try to negotiate.
  -> motherboard_intro

== nine_iron_refuse
  cast: NineIron, Player

NINEIRON
  Then walk. The door's open. Take it.

  When the lights stutter — when you're somewhere else and the lights
  stutter — that'll be it. I won't have done it. You won't have done
  it. Nobody will have. That's the trick of it.

-> ending_walked
